        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "5. Lossless Join & Dependency Preservation",
          "items": [
            "**Lossless join:** rejoin tables without losing or adding tuples",
            "**Dependency preservation:** every FD stays checkable after the split",
            "**Goal:** less redundancy and fewer anomalies, data still recoverable"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Form",
            "Removes",
            "Test"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1NF",
              "non-atomic values",
              "every cell atomic"
            ],
            [
              "2NF",
              "partial dependency",
              "whole-key dependence"
            ],
            [
              "3NF",
              "transitive dependency",
              "PK-only dependence"
            ],
            [
              "BCNF",
              "bad determinants",
              "every X is a super key"
            ],
            [
              "4NF",
              "multi-valued dependency",
              "no independent ->>"
            ],
            [
              "5NF",
              "join dependency",
              "no lossless split left"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "**4. Commands:** `COMMIT` saves all changes permanently",
            "`ROLLBACK` undoes all changes of the transaction",
            "`SAVEPOINT` marks a point inside a transaction",
            "`ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT` undoes changes after that point",
            "`RELEASE SAVEPOINT` removes a savepoint"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SAVEPOINT sp1;",
            "-- do some operations",
            "SAVEPOINT sp2;",
            "-- more operations",
            "ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT sp1;"
          ],
          "note": "rollback to sp1 also destroys sp2"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "layers",
      "subtitle": "3NF, BCNF, 4NF, 5NF"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "4NF, 5NF & Lossless Joins (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "☆ Savepoint Rule",
          "text": "`ROLLBACK TO sp1` ==destroys every savepoint created after sp1==. A later `RELEASE SAVEPOINT sp2` then **fails** — MySQL raises `ERROR 1305: SAVEPOINT sp2 does not exist`; PostgreSQL and Oracle behave the same."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true,
      "hero": "layers",
      "subtitle": "3NF, BCNF, 4NF, 5NF"
